# Mobile app (Expo) environment variables — DEVELOPMENT ONLY.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (Expo loads it automatically for `expo start`
# — no extra package needed) and set EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL to your
# development machine's LAN IP, NOT localhost/127.0.0.1:
#
#   localhost on a physical phone or an Android emulator means THE PHONE
#   itself — there is never a server listening there. Find your machine's
#   LAN IP (macOS/Linux: `ipconfig getifaddr en0` or `hostname -I`;
#   Windows: `ipconfig`) and the phone must be on the same Wi-Fi network.
#
# With no .env file and no shell-exported EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL, the
# app falls back to http://localhost:4000/api automatically (fine ONLY
# for `expo start --web` in this same sandbox/machine, or the iOS
# Simulator specifically, which shares the host's loopback — an Android
# emulator and any physical device both need the real LAN IP below).
# When this fallback is active, the app shows a "MODE DÉV" banner at the
# top of the screen so it's never mistaken for a working connection.
#
# PRODUCTION builds (`eas build`) do NOT read this file — see eas.json's
# per-profile `env` block instead. A production build with no API URL
# configured shows a clear configuration-error screen instead of trying
# localhost (see lib/config.ts).

EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://<your-machine-lan-ip>:4000/api

# Optional — only needed if Socket.IO should point somewhere other than
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL with its trailing /api stripped.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SOCKET_URL=http://<your-machine-lan-ip>:4000
